#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:12
msgid "**Today you will learn to:**"
msgstr "**Днес ще се научите да:**"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:14
msgid "say what is \"true\" and \"false\" in Python, and compare values without surprises;"
msgstr "казвате кое е \"вярно\" и кое \"невярно\" в Python и сравнявате стойности без изненади;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:15
msgid "combine conditions with `and`, `or`, `not`;"
msgstr "комбинирате условия с `and`, `or`, `not`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:16
msgid "write decisions with `if` / `elif` / `else` - the Python `CASE WHEN`;"
msgstr "пишете решения с `if` / `elif` / `else` - `CASE WHEN` на Python;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:17
msgid "choose a value with a conditional expression, and a branch with `match`;"
msgstr "избирате стойност с условен израз, а разклонение - с `match`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:18
msgid "repeat work with `while` and `for`, and stop or skip with `break` and `continue`;"
msgstr "повтаряте работа с `while` и `for` и спирате или прескачате с `break` и `continue`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:19
msgid "loop over the rows of a file, the way a DATA step reads a data set;"
msgstr "обхождате с loop редовете на файл, както DATA step чете набор от данни;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:20
msgid "build a small report and a repayment schedule with loops."
msgstr "съставяте малък отчет и погасителен план с loops."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:22
msgid "From SQL to Python - the same question, two ways:"
msgstr "От SQL към Python - един и същ въпрос, по два начина:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:56
msgid "By the end of today you will be able to read every line of this example. In session 15 pandas does the same in two lines - but it does exactly this inside."
msgstr "До края на днешното занятие ще можете да прочетете всеки ред от този пример. В занятие 15 pandas прави същото с два реда - но отвътре прави точно това."

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:59
msgid "1. True and False"
msgstr "1. True и False"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:61
msgid "The type `bool`"
msgstr "Типът `bool`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:63
msgid "A **Boolean** value (after the mathematician [George Boole](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Boole)) is one of two values: `True` or `False`. They are values, like `0` and `1` - not names of variables. Note the capital letters."
msgstr "**Булевата** стойност (на името на математика [Джордж Бул](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Boole)) е една от две стойности: `True` или `False`. Те са стойности, като `0` и `1` - а не имена на променливи. Обърнете внимание на главните букви."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:73
msgid "Booleans are the result of comparisons (section 2) and the input of every decision (sections 4 - 8) and of every `while` loop (section 11)."
msgstr "Булевите стойности са резултатът от сравненията (раздел 2) и входът на всяко решение (раздели 4 - 8) и на всеки `while` loop (раздел 11)."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:76
msgid "What is true and what is false"
msgstr "Кое е вярно и кое невярно"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:78
msgid "`if` and `while` accept **any value**, not only `True` and `False`. Python decides by the rules you met in session 1 (*truthy* and *falsy*):"
msgstr "`if` и `while` приемат **всяка стойност**, не само `True` и `False`. Python решава по правилата, които видяхте в занятие 1 (*truthy* и *falsy*):"

